$ABCD$ is a kite with $AB=AD$ and $CB=CD$. Its diagonals meet at $M$. The marked angle at $B$ is the whole angle $ABC$. Find:

a. $AD$ and $CD$ in terms of $p$ and $q$

b. $\angle BMC$

c. $\angle ADC$ and $\angle BCD$

d. $\angle BCM$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles,quotes}
\coordinate (A) at (-2,0);\coordinate (B) at (0,-2);\coordinate (C) at (3.464101616,0);\coordinate (D) at (0,2);\coordinate (M) at (0,0);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway,below left] {$p\text{ cm}$};\draw (B)--(C) node[midway,below right] {$q\text{ cm}$};\draw (C)--(D)--(A);
\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);\draw[dashed] (B)--(D);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};\node[below] at (B) {$B$};\node[right] at (C) {$C$};\node[above] at (D) {$D$};\node[above right] at (M) {$M$};
\pic[draw,"$90^\circ$",angle radius=5mm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=B--A--D};
\pic[draw,"$105^\circ$",angle radius=5mm,angle eccentricity=1.8] {angle=C--B--A};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
a. $AD=AB=p\text{ cm}$ and $CD=CB=q\text{ cm}$ (the given pairs of sides are equal).

b. $\angle BMC=90^\circ$ (the diagonals of a kite meet at right angles).

c. $\angle ADC=105^\circ$ (the angles between the unequal sides of a kite are equal).

The interior angles of a quadrilateral add to $360^\circ$.

$\begin{aligned}\angle BCD&=360^\circ-90^\circ-105^\circ-105^\circ\\&=60^\circ\end{aligned}$

d. $\angle BCM=60^\circ\div2=30^\circ$ (the axis $AC$ bisects the angle at $C$).

