$WXYZ$ is a square of side length $6\text{ cm}$, and $WXT$ is an equilateral triangle inside it. Find the smaller angle $XTY$ and the reflex angle $YTZ$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (W) at (0,0);\coordinate (X) at (4,0);\coordinate (Y) at (4,4);\coordinate (Z) at (0,4);\coordinate (T) at (2,3.464101615);
\draw (W)--(X) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ cm}$};\draw (X)--(Y)--(Z)--(W);
\draw (W)--(T)--(X);\draw (Y)--(T)--(Z);
\node[below left] at (W) {$W$};\node[below right] at (X) {$X$};\node[above right] at (Y) {$Y$};\node[above left] at (Z) {$Z$};\node[below] at (T) {$T$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
$\angle TXY=90^\circ-60^\circ=30^\circ$ (a square angle less an equilateral triangle angle).

$XT=WX=XY=6\text{ cm}$, so $\triangle XTY$ is isosceles.

$\begin{aligned}\angle XTY&=(180^\circ-30^\circ)\div2\\&=75^\circ\end{aligned}$

Base angles of an isosceles triangle are equal and its angles add to $180^\circ$.

Similarly, $WT=WZ$, so $\angle ZTW=75^\circ$.

Angles at $T$ add to $360^\circ$.

$\begin{aligned}\text{smaller }\angle YTZ&=360^\circ-75^\circ-60^\circ-75^\circ\\&=150^\circ\end{aligned}$

$\text{reflex }\angle YTZ=360^\circ-150^\circ=210^\circ$.

